            {
              "id": "a402baa7-ba29-3760-b77f-98ccbc0111b1",
              "help": {
                "text": "",
                "markdown": "This finding is considered a genuine vulnerability because the classification indicates a risk of undefined behavior due to the possibility that the destination buffer may be null, and there are no obvious null pointer checks before the buffer operation. The verdict for this call site is also marked as 'GENUINE', confirming the high confidence in the issue. The source is a string literal, which is always valid, but the destination buffer could be null, leading to a potential crash or undefined behavior if the function is called with a null pointer. There are no explicit guards or null-termination after the copy, and the buffer size is not derived from the destination's capacity. These factors all contribute to the assessment that this is a real and actionable issue.\n\n## In Context Remediation 1\nBefore performing the copy operation, ensure that the destination buffer is not null. Add an explicit check to prevent undefined behavior if the pointer is null.\n\n```cpp\nif (event_ntfn_data.message != nullptr) {\n    strncpy(event_ntfn_data.message, \"test event\", MAX_EVENT_NOTIFICATION_MSG_SIZE);\n    // Optionally, ensure null-termination:\n    event_ntfn_data.message[MAX_EVENT_NOTIFICATION_MSG_SIZE - 1] = '\\0';\n}\n```\n\nThis prevents the function from attempting to write to a null pointer, which would otherwise cause a crash or undefined behavior.\n\n## In Context Remediation 2\nIf the destination buffer is a member of a struct and should never be null, ensure that the struct is always properly initialized before use. If the pointer can be null by design, consider handling the error case explicitly:\n\n```cpp\nif (!event_ntfn_data.message) {\n    // Handle error: destination buffer is null\n    // Log, return error, or take appropriate action\n} else {\n    strncpy(event_ntfn_data.message, \"test event\", MAX_EVENT_NOTIFICATION_MSG_SIZE);\n    event_ntfn_data.message[MAX_EVENT_NOTIFICATION_MSG_SIZE - 1] = '\\0';\n}\n```\n\n## References\n- [OWASP C-Based Toolchain Hardening Cheat Sheet](https://cheatsheetseries.owasp.org/cheatsheets/C-Based_Toolchain_Hardening_Cheat_Sheet.html)\n- [CWE-476: NULL Pointer Dereference](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/476.html)\n- [OWASP Buffer Overflow](https://owasp.org/www-community/vulnerabilities/Buffer_Overflow)\n- [NIST Buffer Overflow](https://csrc.nist.gov/glossary/term/buffer_overflow)\n\n___\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "tags": [
                  "DS111237"
                ]
              }
